    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **25 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` derived field on the owner response.\n\nThe owner response DTO is generated from the OpenAPI spec, and derived fields (like `membershipNumber`) are computed in the MapStruct mapper \u2014 I followed that existing pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property (enum `SILVER`/`BRONZE`) to the owner response schema, so the generator produces an `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression and a `membershipTier(owner)` helper: returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` **and** an email is present (non-null, non-blank), otherwise `BRONZE`.\n\nThe rule reads the already-persisted `namesakeCount` (assigned at create by `AssignNamesakeCount`) and the owner's own `email`, mirroring how `membershipNumber` derives from owner fields. Both new tests (`Cp15Tests`: SILVER for unique-name-with-email, BRONZE for no-email) pass, and no existing tests regressed.",
